    <!-- ─── SEO FAQ ACCORDIONS (MATCHES FAQPAGE SCHEMA) ─── -->
    <section class="seo-section reveal" id="faq">
        <div class="sec-header">
            <div>
                <span class="sec-label">Knowledge Base</span>
                <h2 class="sec-title">Dark Psychology <em>FAQ</em></h2>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-grid">
            <details class="faq">
                <summary>What is dark psychology?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Dark psychology is the study of how people use manipulation, coercion, and deception to influence others for their own benefit. It draws on research into the dark triad (narcissism, Machiavellianism, and psychopathy) and helps readers recognize and resist these tactics.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>What is the best dark psychology book for beginners?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Dark Psychology by Jonathan Mind and Read People Like a Book by Patrick King are our top beginner recommendations. They explain manipulation tactics in plain language, use real-world examples from everyday life, and provide practical defensive techniques.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>Is dark psychology real or a myth?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Dark psychology is a popular descriptor rather than a formal academic degree, but the behaviors it covers are deeply researched. Studies on the dark triad, coercive control, and persuasion science provide the scientific foundation for understanding these tactics.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>Is it ethical to read books about manipulation?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Yes, reading about manipulation is ethical and often protective. Understanding tactics like gaslighting and covert persuasion makes you far harder to exploit. Our library focuses on awareness, boundary-setting, and defense, not harming others.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>What are the most common manipulation tactics?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    The most common manipulation tactics are gaslighting, love bombing, guilt-tripping, triangulation, the silent treatment, foot-in-the-door requests, and manufactured scarcity. Each one exploits normal human emotional needs and cognitive vulnerabilities.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>What is the difference between persuasion and manipulation?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Persuasion openly appeals to someone's reasoning and leaves them free to say no, while manipulation conceals intent and exploits weaknesses. A good test: would the tactic still work if the other person knew exactly what you were doing?
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>Which dark psychology books cover narcissism and gaslighting?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Gaslighting - 4 Books in 1 and Dark Psychology and Manipulation directly address narcissism and gaslighting. They walk through narcissistic abuse cycles, explain covert escalation, and provide boundary scripts to disengage safely.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>What formats are available in this dark psychology library?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Most dark psychology books in our library are available in digital PDF, EPUB, and MOBI formats for direct reading on phones, e-readers, tablets, and desktop computers.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>How do I download or access books from the library?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Simply browse the library grid, click on any title to view details, and click download or read online to verify access. Digital access is instant and free.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>Can dark psychology books help in relationships or at work?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Yes, dark psychology books help you spot manipulation in personal relationships and office politics before it causes damage. Readers use them to handle manipulative colleagues, recognize toxic partners, and negotiate boundaries.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>What is the Dark Triad in psychology?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    The Dark Triad comprises three overlapping personality traits: Narcissism (grandiosity and entitlement), Machiavellianism (strategic deceit and self-interest), and Psychopathy (impulsivity and callous lack of empathy).
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq">
                <summary>Why does PsychoSculpt focus on defensive psychological knowledge?</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    We believe psychological literacy protects personal sovereignty. Learning how coercive influence functions allows readers to establish unshakeable boundaries and resist deception in daily life.
                </div>
            </details>
        </div>
    </section>

